{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Design decision (standing authorization): reduce the per-read probe by checking durable store structure before falling back to git HEAD, not by caching. Rationale: common active OSS practice is to avoid caching health predicates that must notice filesystem state changes; a committed on-disk sentinel is a cheap live check. This keeps marker-only and mid-clone stores loud, keeps gitless snapshots readable, and removes the steady-state git spawn for initialized stores."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788830206555831001,"uuid":"e0423395-bfd4-49da-b29d-102435a19026"}